# Wolfen

## Lore

The Wolfen are the most civilized and powerful of the Palladium World''s three canine races: giant wolf-headed warriors, 7 to 10 feet tall and 350 to 500 pounds, covered in dark or light grey fur, with hazel, brown or green eyes. Only in the last two or three generations have their feuding tribes united into a disciplined military society that looks remarkably like early Rome, down to garb, weapons and tactics. Human settlers pushing north on Palladium have brought the two peoples to the edge of war.

On Rifts Earth they are rare - lone warriors and small bands, and rumors of a Roman-style canine culture repopulating Italy that nobody has confirmed. In North America a Wolfen is usually taken for a Dog Boy, though it stands far taller, has true animal haunches, speaks and writes its own language and shows an independence Dog Boys rarely do. In Canada, France, Russia and Eastern Europe they are mistaken for Loup Garou, werewolves, demons or woodland spirits.

**Alignment:** Any, but tends toward Principled and Aberrant, both of which carry a strong personal code of honor.

**Average Life Span:** 60+ years. A Wolfen gives birth to 1D4 young after an eight-month gestation and reaches full maturity at 13.

## GM Notes

Being soldiers by nature, Wolfen think M.D.C. body armor and M.D. weapons are marvelous inventions, and most strive for a full suit sized to them. They favor large swords, pole arms and battle axes, and on Rifts Earth Vibro-Blades and energy weapons of every kind.

Traditionally they despise humans, Dwarves and Changelings; they count Elves as enemies for their alliance with humans while coveting Elven friendship. They regard the supernatural as dangerous. Free Wolfen view loyalist Dog Boys with puzzlement rather than contempt, and Dog Boys see them as dangerous feral cousins.
